LeftOpen modifies the bundled CLI and hosts module:
- separate launchd label and hosts-file markers, leaving external Portless alone;
- expose a read-only project-info command using upstream inference and config;
- expire native-observed routes and recheck owner liveness on every request.
Proxying, certificates, HTTP/2, WebSockets, project launch, worktree naming,
framework port injection, and service management remain upstream Portless implementations.
